# wecms-web environment configuration — TEMPLATE
# Copy to `.env.local` (local dev) or set per-environment at deploy time.
# This is the only env file tracked by git (`.gitignore` ignores `.env*`
# except `.env.example`); real values live in gitignored `.env.local` /
# deploy-time env so each environment points at its own backend.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL
#   Origin of the wecms-api backend the BROWSER calls directly (Axios
#   baseURL — see lib/axios.ts). `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is inlined by Next.js at
#   BUILD TIME, so it must be set before `next build` / `next dev`.
#
#   When unset, lib/axios.ts falls back to `http://localhost:8080`. That
#   only works when the browser and the backend share one machine (local
#   dev). A DEPLOYED frontend with this UNSET makes the browser try the
#   *viewer's* localhost:8080 -> request fails -> the page silently falls
#   back to mock data (root cause in
#   docs/features/banking/reports/daily-financial/runtime-data-source-check.md).
#
#   Per-environment values (frontend origin -> backend origin):
#     Local dev        http://localhost:3000           -> http://localhost:8080
#     Coocon sample    http://sample.coocon.co.kr:3000 -> http://sample.coocon.co.kr:8080
#     SIT              https://wecms.kosign.dev        -> https://wecms-api.kosign.dev
#
#   A shell / CI environment variable of the same name OVERRIDES this file,
#   so deploy pipelines set the correct value per target without editing it.
#   Backend CORS already whitelists the three frontend origins above
#   (wecms-api application-local.yml `wecms.cors.allowed-origins`).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
